      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:1:2:20:10",
      "text": [
        " قُلْتُ لَهُ أَ كُلُّ شَيْ‏ءٍ فِي كِتَابِ اللَّهِ وَ سُنَّةِ نَبِيِّهِ ( صلى الله عليه وآله ) أَوْ تَقُولُونَ فِيهِ قَالَ بَلْ كُلُّ شَيْ‏ءٍ فِي كِتَابِ اللَّهِ وَ سُنَّةِ نَبِيِّهِ ( صلى الله عليه وآله ) ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "A number of our companions, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad Bin Khalid, from Ismail Bin Mihran, from Sayf Bin Ameyra, from Abu Magra’a, from Sama’at, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Al-Hassan Musa<sup>asws</sup>, said, ‘I said to him<sup>asws</sup>, ‘Is everything in the Book of Allah<sup>azwj</sup> and the Sunnah of His<sup>azwj</sup> Prophet<sup>saww</sup>, or are you<sup>asws</sup> (Imams<sup>asws</sup>) are saying with regards to it?’ He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘But, everything is in the Book of Allah<sup>azwj</sup> and the Sunnah from His<sup>azwj</sup> Prophet<sup>saww</sup>’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          " 9. A number of our people has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn ‘Isa from Ali ibn Ni‘man from ’Isma‘il ibn Jabir from abu ‘Abdallah (a.s.) who has said the following. “In the book of Allah there is the news of things before you, the reports of the matters after you and the laws to settle your disputes and we know it all.”"
        ]
      }
    },
